# Cursor Rules for BanjaraBio Flutter Project

## 🚨 CRITICAL: Memory Leak Prevention

**⚠️ MANDATORY: Before making ANY code changes, read:**
- `MEMORY_LEAK_PREVENTION.md` - Complete guide for preventing memory leaks

**All AI assistants MUST follow the rules in `MEMORY_LEAK_PREVENTION.md` when:**
- Creating new widgets/screens
- Modifying existing code
- Refactoring components
- Adding new features

**Key Rules (see full guide for details):**
- Always cancel StreamSubscriptions in dispose()
- Always cancel Timers in dispose()
- Always dispose Controllers and remove listeners
- Always add timeout protection to Completers
- Always unsubscribe RealtimeChannels
- Always close ReceivePorts
- Never dispose singletons from individual widgets

---

## Cursor Editor Optimization

### Memory Management
- Always use const constructors where possible
- Avoid unnecessary rebuilds
- Use RepaintBoundary for complex widgets
- Limit file watching to active files only

### Code Analysis
- Disable semantic highlighting in Cursor settings
- Reduce code lens and minimap rendering
- Limit analysis to active files when possible

### Build Optimization
- Use incremental builds
- Clean build cache regularly
- Avoid full project rebuilds
